\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys dollars at 5.00  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 253 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2005\par 15:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds dealers' comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday continued its almost daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the tightly controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollars at 5.00 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  compared with 5.01 on the previous trading day.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had set its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  volume at $30 million, up from Tuesday's $10 million.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said demand for dollars was slowly rising but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  with dollar purchases to help commercial banks cover orders left from the previous trading day when the volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was too low.  \par \par \uc2 "There were not only dollar sellers today but also buyers," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts as a clearance house for the market as commercial banks are not allowed to buy and sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same trading day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long promised to free up the market but has done little to ease its grip.  \par \par \uc2 Interbank deals were being struck at 4.99-5.00 on Wednesday, roughly the same as on the previous trading day and down from last week's levels of 4.965-4.97.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been committed to a policy of preventing any sharp upward \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement to protect the interests of exporters -- the engine of economic growth. A bank official has said this month the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was "optimal".  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 HRYVNIA\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050831e18v001eq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
