\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  c.bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 ,  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  rate unchanged  \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 August 2005\par 13:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday maintained its almost daily \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market it controls closely, buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the seventh consecutive session.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said dollar supply still outpaced demand as it has for weeks, but demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had risen over last week's sessions. There was no immediate explanation for the increase in demand for dollars.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still buying dollars but the market was fairly even today, with (dollar) supply down a bit," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "Demand was rising already on Friday, but this had only a minimal effect on the rate. Today, there was some movement."  \par \par \uc2 He suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might cease its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming days.  \par \par \uc2 Interbank deals were being struck at 4.985-4.997, with the dollar climbing from last week's levels of 4.965-4.97.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been committed to a policy of preventing any sharp upward movement of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect the interests of exporters -- the engine of economic growth. A bank official last week said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate was "optimal".  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed to follow through on pledges to liberalise strict rules for market participants despite appeals from President Viktor Yushchenko, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers and the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday announced its proposed rates for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- 5.00 to 5.06 -- only minutes before actually proceeding with purchases -- and not at the beginning of the session as it did through most of last week.  \par \par \uc2 It also reduced its volume of proposed purchases to $20 million from $35 million last week.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said it was difficult to determine whether increased demand for dollars stemmed from rising imports or non-residents withdrawing from the market.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no clear immediate reason," said one dealer. "And it is difficult to say whether it will continue to rise or is only a short-term phenomenon."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050829e18t000rb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
