\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , official says rate optimal  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 515 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 August 2005\par 09:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds comments by top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 25 (Reuters) - The Ukraine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday resumed purchases of dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market it tightly controls and a top bank official described as "optimal" the rate of Ukraine's hyrvnia \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it has been defending.  \par \par \uc2 Anatoly Shapovalov, the bank's first deputy chairman, also predicted demand for dollars, now exceeded by supply, would soon pick up as autumn weather prompted energy purchases. He said the bank had enough reserves to prevent sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fifth consecutive session as it sought to uphold a competitive exchange rate for exporters.  \par \par \uc2 "Today we had what is now the standard situation," said one dealer. "Dollar supply exceeded demand and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought at 5.0 to the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 He said interbank deals were being struck at 4.97-4.995 -- as the market reopened after the Independence Day holiday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has long been committed to avoiding abrupt upward movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It oversaw a one-day three percent rise in late April, sapping market confidence, and has since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly every day to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was only buying receipts from exporters. Other customers had to sell dollars more cheaply.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had concluded that it had found the right level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "There is pressure now but this is not coming from export earnings," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "We therefore look at the structure of inflows and conclude that this is the optimal rate. We look to see whether there is borrowing, credits, non-residents' funds. And there is no basis for a strengthening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 DEMAND FOR DOLLARS TO RISE  \par \par \uc2 Energy purchases in the autumn would "naturally push up demand. But I believe the reserves we have accumulated will be sufficient to prevent any sharp changes."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched trading with its now standard practice of issuing parameters for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.0/5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar and set the indicative volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $35 million. The market opened at 4.9740/4.9980.  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers say attempts to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within certain limits would run up against a growing supply of dollars, particularly a probable influx of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to plans to stage new privatisations of big industrial sites.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed to make good on promises to liberalise market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite appeals from President Viktor Yushchenko, dealers and the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's former deputy head, Serhiy Yaryomenko, an advocate of tight market control who quit last week, told the daily Ekonomicheskiye Izvestiya that abandoning regulation would fuel inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "A rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could stimulate inflation," he told the daily. "People will turn away from foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on grounds that it has suddenly got cheaper and start buying property and durable goods."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050825e18p001ca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
