\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Ukraine C.Bank accuses banks of attacking  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 August 2005\par 10:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds more comment, fresh \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 23 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday accused a number of banks with foreign capital of launching speculative attacks on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and threatened to bar them from the market unless they stopped.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , committed for months to avoiding abrupt upward movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on the market it closely controls, buying dollars at 5.0 -- a rate unchanged for four sessions.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  statement accused the banks of hatching a "plot" to destabilise the market by trying to sell unreasonable amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers dismissed the statement as groundless and unhelpful. Some described it as little more than bluster.  \par \par \uc2 "An analysis of events in recent months on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market shows that specific banks have been trying to conduct improper \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  by offering to sell large amounts of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  which they did not have available," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in the statement on its website  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bank.gov.ua"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bank.gov.ua }}}\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Unfortunately, such actions are mainly carried out by specific Ukrainian banks with foreign capital, in agreement with foreign banks," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added. It did not name any banks.  \par \par \uc2 "This can be seen as a plot aimed not so much at benefitting from speculation but rather at driving the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market into instability and fuelling inflation."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it viewed these actions as "speculative attacks with the aim of deliberately destabilising the rate of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".  \par \par \uc2 Out of an overall total of 163 banks in Ukraine, 22 have foreign capital including nine which are 100 percent foreign-owned.  \par \par \uc2 "This is a particularly heavy-handed way of verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sonal Desai, analyst at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein in Milan. "There's an escalation in rhetoric, which is trying to prevent the inflows from occurring."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMISTS BLAME \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Lars Christensen, senior economist at Danske Bank, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no one to blame but itself.  \par \par \uc2 "The problems for monetary policy in Ukraine have not been created by 'the market' or 'speculators', but rather by outdated and untransparent policies of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Sergei Voloboyev, emerging markets economist at CSFB in London was equally blunt: "This statement is an example of what the market would not want a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do when it is under pressure. It is unfortunately not a constructive approach."  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers at banks in Ukraine with foreign capital were even more vocal in criticism.  \par \par \uc2 "What sort of crime is this?" said one. "Every investor wants to sell dear and buy cheap."  \par \par \uc2 "We are breaking no regulations," said another. "Perhaps it's aimed at intimidating someone or other."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  engineered a one-day three percent rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late April, sapping confidence in the market, and has since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  nearly every day to keep it steady.  \par \par \uc2 It has bought dollars at 5.00 since last Thursday, a slight weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 4.99 and 4.98. And the bank has since last week adopted a practice of announcing early in the session parameters for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said attempts to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within certain limits would run up against a growing supply of dollars, particularly a probable influx of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to plans for new privatisations of big industrial sites.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed to make good on promises to liberalise market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  despite appeals from President Viktor Yushchenko, dealers and the International Monetary Fund.  \par \par \uc2 A government minister welcomed the resignation last week of a top bank official who wanted to maintain tight restrictions -- including a ban on buying and selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same day.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Douglas Busvine and Meg Clothier in Moscow and Sujata Rao in London)  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-CENTRALBANK (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN