\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  C.Bank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2 , keeps  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 August 2005\par 16:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (New story with dealer comment)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 19 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as it has done every day this week, keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady despite low demand for dollars.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bank's action amounted to an assurance that Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be allowed to rise sharply, contrary to expectations after this week's resignation of a top official who advocated continued strict controls over the market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars on Friday at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- the same rate as at the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 And for the second day running, it announced in advance the parameters it intended to use for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the trading session -- a \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 5.00/5.06 to the dollar and a total volume of $40 million.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also bought at 5.0 on Thursday -- a slight weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 4.99 on Wednesday and 4.98 at the week's first two sessions.  \par \par \uc2 "In objective terms, the supply of dollars exceeds demand. But we see no rise in the rate for \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases of dollars or even conditions for that to happen," said one dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "This is psychological pressure on the market so that the market does not start thinking that the dollar will plunge."  \par \par \uc2 Market participants said that initial trades were conducted close to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. But the dollar began to slip as supply rose, with some trades noted at 4.95. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came at the close of the session.  \par \par \uc2 "The market thought the departure of (deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Serhiy) Yaryomenko, an opponent of a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would result in it climbing sharply," said a dealer.  \par \par \uc2 "But what we're seeing indicates that they are trying very hard to ensure that doesn't happen, to keep the rate steady."  \par \par \uc2 CALLS TO LIBERALISE RULES  \par \par \uc2 Dealers have complained at a lack of predictability of rates. Many said the bank's failure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly last week prompted a sharp rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a time, causing panic among exporters, the main engine behind economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers, ministers and the International Monetary Fund have called for a liberalisation of the trading rules. Ukrainian President Viktor Yushchenko last week told \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Viktor Stelmakh to draft proposals quickly to change the rules.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers say that if banks were allowed to conduct arbitrage deals or use other instruments, imbalances would be avoided.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has failed since May to make good on promises to ease restrictions, including a ban on banks buying and selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same day.  \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Serhiy Teryokhin said on Thursday that the deputy chairman's departure would make it easier to bring about changes together with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Some dealers said attempts to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  within certain limits would run up against a growing supply of dollars.  \par \par \uc2 "What is really happening is minimal demand and considerable supply of dollars. And this is likely to intensify," said one, citing a probable influx of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to plans for privatisations of the Kryvorizhstal steel mill and the Nikopol ferro-alloy maker.  \par \par \uc2 Premier Yulia Tymoshenko has said the Kryvorizhstal sale could fetch as much as $3 billion.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|BNX|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050819e18j001h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
