\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Ukraine c.bank posts  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  rate, dollar creeps up  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 600 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2005\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds comments by economy minister)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday in the country's tightly controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, overseeing a slight weakening in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the second day running by buying dollars at 5.0 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Economy Minister Serhiy Teryokhin, meanwhile, said the resignation this week of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy chairman, an advocate of strict controls over the market, would facilitate the government's work with the bank.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the fourth in as many days this week on the exchange, was conducted as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  changed its tactics by announcing its intentions beforehand. Dealers said that offered at least a measure of predictability previously lacking.  \par \par \uc2 "From the very outset of trading, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  put up a declared rate of 5.0 and stated its intention of buying $40 million," said one dealer. "It then acted strictly in keeping with that declaration."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 4.99 on Wednesday and at 4.98 at the two previous sessions. Last week, the bank had allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise slowly after trying to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.01 to the dollar since late April.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said it was hard to understand why the bank was now allowing the dollar to creep upward against the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But they said the bank's action set a framework for a slight rise in the dollar with little chance of major fluctuations.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made it clear it was going to buy at 5.0 and people fell into line by selling around that 5.0 mark," said one market participant from a bank with foreign capital.  \par \par \uc2 "At least the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set out its intentions," said another dealer. "That makes matters a bit easier. We have a framework."  \par \par \uc2 NEW PRACTICE?  \par \par \uc2 But dealers said it was unclear whether Thursday's move was a one-off or would become standard bank practice.  \par \par \uc2 Teryokhin told reporters the departure of deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Serhiy Yaryomenko, would make it easier to work out proposals to liberalise the exchange market.  \par \par \uc2 "I believe that work with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will go more smoothly," Teryokhin said.  \par \par \uc2 He said government officials had already met with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to discuss monetary policy, stable levels for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and proposals to liberalise market rules.  \par \par \uc2 About 10 proposals were in the works, among them the creation of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  corridor to make movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value more predictable.  \par \par \uc2 Bank chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh has so far given no indication of how he intends to respond to Ukrainian President Viktor Yushchenko's calls for rapid liberalisation.  \par \par \uc2 Market participants had been expressing considerable unease at the unpredictability of rates on the market and called for the easing of restrictions for banks.  \par \par \uc2 Many said the bank's failure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a timely manner last week prompted a sharp rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a time, sowing panic among exporters who are the main engine behind economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers say that if banks were allowed to conduct arbitrage deals or use other instruments, market imbalances would be avoided.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has failed since May to make good on promises to ease restrictions, including a ban on banks buying and selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same day.  \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund has sought both liberalisation and curbs on money supply to tackle inflation -- now running at 15 percent.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050818e18i00199\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
