\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine C.Bank buys dollars at same rate as Friday  \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 August 2005\par 15:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds background)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market it closely controls on Monday, buying dollars at 4.98 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the same rate as Friday.  \par \par \uc2 "There was considerable supply of dollars and not many buyers," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  four days in a row last week, in effect allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drift slowly upward after it broke through the barrier of 5 to the dollar. It bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 4.99 on Thursday and 4.98 on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is at its highest level since 1999.  \par \par \uc2 For weeks, the bank tried to hold the rate at 5.01 after engineering a three percent rise in its value in a single day, undermining confidence in the market.  \par \par \uc2 Officials say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh is to make a statement outlining \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy in the coming days. Dealers last week said the bank had made incomprehensible moves, including a delay in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise slowly.  \par \par \uc2 President Viktor Yushchenko last week told Stelmakh to draft proposals to liberalise the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by removing restrictions imposed on banks and allowing enterprises greater freedom to use \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers say that if banks were allowed to conduct arbitrage deals or use other instruments, the market could avoid both imbalances requiring \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and big swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's value.  \par \par \uc2 The bank has promised since May to ease restrictions, including a ban on banks buying and selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same day, but has not taken the necessary decisions.  \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund has urged Ukraine to curb money supply growth and ease its grip on the exchange rate to tackle inflation now running at 15 percent.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050815e18f0012p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
