\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 4- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 , lets  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalya Zinets  \par \uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 August 2005\par 10:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds president's statement)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, Aug 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its tightly controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Thursday, but allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise gently by buying dollars more cheaply than in previous sessions.  \par \par \uc2 With the market plunged into turmoil this week by what dealers described as incomprehensible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, Ukraine's president told its chairman to work with ministers and banks to draft proposals on liberalising its rigid rules.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers this week criticised days of delay in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market, which served only to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher for a time.  \par \par \uc2 They expressed new confusion over the purchase of dollars on Thursday at the new, cheaper rate when upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already eased. Some suggested timely implementation of the bank's actions appeared to depend on political decisions.  \par \par \uc2 Officials announced bank chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh, who met President Viktor Yushchenko at his holiday residence in Crimea, would make a statement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy next week. They pledged there would be no abrupt movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third day in a row to temper a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but bought dollars at a new rate of 4.99 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar instead of the previous 5.01.  \par \par \uc2 "The change in the rate is, of course, no surprise," said a specialist from a bank with foreign capital.  \par \par \uc2 "But up to the last moment, it was hard to believe the bank would make such a move. Any decision on strengthening the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now firmly in the realm of politics."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said it was surprising the bank had embarked on the new rate as of 4.99 as imbalances between dollar supply and demand had eased on Thursday. Interbank deals were being struck at 4.98-5.00 instead of 4.96-.4.90 earlier in the week.  \par \par \uc2 HIGHEST SINCE 1999  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke through the level of 5 to the dollar this week, rising to its highest point since 1999.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has bought about $5 billion on the market this year, has been making purchases at at 5.01 since the end of April after engineering a one-day rise of three percent in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That move badly sapped market confidence.  \par \par \uc2 A statement on Yushchenko's Web site  {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.president.gov.ua"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.president.gov.ua }}}\uc2  said the president had "asked the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in coordination with the government and finance ministry to come up with proposals to liberalise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets".  \par \par \uc2 It said he sought "the removal of specific \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions on banks and measures to enable enterprises to make greater use of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and securities".  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been promising to alter \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May, but has put off all necessary decisions.  \par \par \uc2 The bank resumed \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's upward movement despite calls from the International Monetary Fund to allow a more flexible rate to curb inflation.  \par \par \uc2 "The chairman will explain everything next week," Serhiy Yaremenko, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, told reporters. "I believe the rate will be stable."  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bank's strategy and timing could generate new imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 "Exporters will want to sell more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  more quickly in order not to lose out on the rate," said one dealer. "Buyers will simply hold back with purchases on the notion that the dollar will become cheaper in a few days."  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 4)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050811e18b0012y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
