\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank buys dollars for 10th day  \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juli 2005\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the tightly-controlled \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the 10th day in a row on Thursday, buying dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been buying dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the end of April after it raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by about 3 percent in a single stroke.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already bought about $150 million on the market since the start of July and about $4.6 billion in total since start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts as a clearance house for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and sets the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by administrative means, fixed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.050 to the dollar for Thursday, up from 5.055 previously.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh told Reuters in an interview on Wednesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had no plans to change its exchange rate policy despite having to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets daily to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at its target level.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to buy dollars this month due to higher dollar sales by exporters of steel and grain.  \par \par \uc2 "The supply of dollars is high. The interbank deals are being done at not higher than 5.02 for about two weeks already. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to buy," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "This year Ukraine has a good grain harvest. We can see many grain traders selling dollars at the moment," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine, once the breadbasket of the former Soviet Union, is an active grain exporter and expects a good grain harvest this year after a record crop in 2005.  \par \par \uc2 But from September, the trend may reverse, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "In autumn everything will change. From autumn to spring, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is usually selling dollars to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Such seasonal factors in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  is caused by the structure of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy," said a dealer at a foreign bank in Kiev.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's economy is export-led with key industries of steel and chemicals.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050721e17l001ld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
