\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank in new dollar purchases  \b0\par\par\uc2 353 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juli 2005\par 14:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds more quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, buying dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the seventh day in a row as metal exporters continued high dollar sales, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is buying because a lot of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is offered for sale. But there is nobody else who can buy except the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a dealer at a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 "In recent weeks I do not remember a similiar inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from everywhere. Everybody is selling."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acts as a clearing house for the interbank market because commercial banks are not allowed to both sell and buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single trading day.  \par \par \uc2 The market was more or less balanced in the last two months after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scrapped a requirement for obligatory dollar sales by exporters and raised the value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by about 3 percent in a single stroke in April.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in May and June, both buying and selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , to defend its new target rate of 5.05 to the dollar but the frequency of its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  was less. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $387.1 million in May and sold $10.5 million in June.  \par \par \uc2 Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $100 million, dealers estimated.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the bulk of the hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales was formed by exporters -- steel and other metal companies and grain traders who have already started sales of the new grain harvest.  \par \par \uc2 "Banks traditionally working with the steel sector account for the lion's share of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Ukrainian exporters of steel and other metals, which account for about 40 percent of the country's total exports, have been complaining of late about worsening world market conditions for their products.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine, once the breadbasket of the Soviet Union, also hopes for a good grain harvest this year after a record crop last year.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050718e17i000ea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
