\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys dollars at 5.01  \b0\par\par\uc2 358 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2005\par 15:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, July 6 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market it tightly controls on Wednesday, buying dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> by about 3 percent in a single stroke in April and has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  frequently, both buying and selling the dollar, to defend its new target rate of 5.05 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 It was \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week.  \par \par \uc2 "From July 1, there has been higher dollar supply. Today was the same, supply was higher. It is hard to say who and why has increased dollar sales," said a dealer from a foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 "But I think it is temprorary. The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will slide. To be more exact, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will maintain the rate, but from time to time we will feel shortages of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as was the case in May and June."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 5.0180/5.0350 at the end of the trading day compared with 5.0250/5.0420 in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said its gross hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves slipped to $13.073 billion at the end of June from $13.190 billion in May due to payments to service foreign debt and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 In June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  both sold and bought dollars on the interbank market, its transactions in the end amounting to sales of $10.5 million to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . In May, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $387.1 million on the market.  \par \par \uc2 At the start of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy out dollars and curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise, attributed to robust exports and a steady inflow of foreign funds in Ukraine's domestic debt market.  \par \par \uc2 But conditions on world markets for Ukraine's major exports -- steel and chemicals -- have deteriorated. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government have also scrapped a rule on obligatory dollar sales for exporters and liberalised imports.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050706e176001a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
