\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  cbank hopes reserves stay steady  \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Juni 2005\par 14:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds Thursday \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 30 (Reuters) - A senior Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official on Thursday said he hoped foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves would remain stable at about $13 billion through 2005 and predicted the bank could keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady.  \par \par \uc2 First deputy chairman Anatoly Shapovalov said he believed the reserves level could be maintained despite worsening conditions for Ukrainian exports and high prices for imported natural gas.  \par \par \uc2 "We will hold steady. This is despite forecasts by specialists of worsening conditions on international markets for our export goods -- metals and chemicals -- and predicted higher gas prices.  \par \par \uc2 "At the same time, we have a positive balance of payments of $2.4 billion for the first five months of the year."  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov gave no forecast for the level of reserves in the immediate future. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest figures put gross \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at $13.19 billion at the end of May, down from $13.21 billion on May 23.  \par \par \uc2 Shapovalov also said the the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had "every possibility to keep the (\b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) rate stable through the end of the year".  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market it tightly controls to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  steady, both buying and selling dollars.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday and Thursday it bought dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But in recent weeks, it has tended to sell the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- eight times this month at 5.06.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen as undervalued early in the year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a single day in April by about 3 percent to 5.05 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-UKRAINE-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|BNX|RNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050630e16u001ix\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
