\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  in new dollar sales  \b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2005\par 14:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 17 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 It was the third time this week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold dollars.  \par \par \uc2 "Today, several banks found themselves short of being able to satisfy demand for dollars," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Deals were being done at 5.025/5.04 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ensure that payment for contracts were not put off until next week as Monday is a public holiday.  \par \par \uc2 "Volumes were not especially large and this is not terribly serious," said one dealer. "It actually plays into the hands of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in fighting inflation."  \par \par \uc2 The bank tightly controls the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and acts as a clearance house as commercial banks are not allowed to both sell and buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single trading day.  \par \par \uc2 In the first months of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen as undervalued due to robust exports, a current account surplus and a steady inflow of foreign funds in the domestic debt market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a stroke in April by about 3 percent to 5.05 per dollar from 5.19 and many had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise further.  \par \par \uc2 But the trend is changing due to slower economic growth. In the first weeks of June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to interevene frequently with dollar sales to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has sold dollars at 5.06 since May 31.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050617e16h0018m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
