\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's c. bank sells dollars at 5.06  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2005\par 15:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, selling dollars at 5.06 for the second time this week.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to cover a bid for dollars from a large foreign bank.  \par \par \uc2 "Almost for the entire day demand and supply seemed to be balanced. But then it turned out that one of the big banks could not cover its bid and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably decided to help," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and acts as a clearance house as commercial banks are not allowed both to sell and buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single trading day.  \par \par \uc2 In the first months of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen as undervalued due to robust exports, a sound current account surplus and a steady inflow of foreign funds into the domestic debt market.  \par \par \uc2 In April, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  by about 3 percent to 5.05 per dollar from 5.19 in a single stroke. Many had expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise further.  \par \par \uc2 But the trend is changing due to the slower growth of Ukraine's export-reliant economy, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 In the first weeks of June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to interevene frequently with dollar sales to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has sold dollars at 5.06 since May 31.  \par \par \uc2 Many foreigners who actively bought Ukrainian domestic debt early in the year in anticipation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, have virtually stopped debt purchases now. Some apear willing to withdraw their funds from Ukraine.  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry sold only 14-month paper worth a total of about 120 million \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  ($24 million) at a yield of 5.8 percent at auctions on Tuesday while two-, three- and five-year debt failed to sell due to low yields.  \par \par \uc2 "Growth has slown sharply, inflation is stubbornly high and the current account surplus is falling. Over the past few weeks, the accumulation of reserves effectively came to a halt," CSFB investment bank said in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 "The deterioration in the macroeconomic performance in recent months has reduced the pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to revalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  again."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050615e16f001gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
