\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  buys dollars at 5.01  \b0\par\par\uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 2005\par 13:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds dealer quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Friday, buying dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in the last three weeks, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 "It seemed there was demand for the dollar for most of the day but it turned out that a few large sellers were still on the market in afternoon trade," said a dealer at a leading Ukrainian bank.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightly controls the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and acts as a clearance house as commercial banks are not allowed both to sell and buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single trading day.  \par \par \uc2 The last time it bought dollars was on May 19.  \par \par \uc2 Over the last three weeks the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to defend its target rate of 5.05 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar set on Apr. 21 following the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's three percent rise in one day.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise, yielding under a pressure of a steady inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the country from exporters and foreign investors, putting monet into the domestic debt market.  \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund has urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier this week to allow a greater exchange rate flexibility, saying it was a key to bring down spiralling inflation to single digit this year.  \par \par \uc2 The government plans to limit inflation to 9.8 percent this year from 12.3 percent in 2004. Annual inflation doubled to 14 percent in January to May.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has promised to free up the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market but has been delaying decisions so far.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to continue to buy dollars but the amount and frequency of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  would fall compared with the first months of the year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already bought $4.6 billion since the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 "The situation with Ukrainian exports is not as good as it used to be," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|UKI|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050610e16a0011k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
