\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine resumes dollar sales to shore up  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juni 2005\par 14:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Adds quotes from dealers, background on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 6 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed dollar sales to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has spent much of the past two months \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars and check the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. But it changed tack last week and started selling dollars as the rising fuel imports drove up demand for U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Today we saw slightly higher demand on the market. A couple of big banks wanted to buy dollars and created all the demand," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tightly controls the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and acts as a market clearing house as commercial banks are not allowed both to buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a single trading day.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine, which depends heavily on Russian energy imports, was hit last month by rising fuel prices, shortages and queues at petrol pumps.  \par \par \uc2 The government scrapped duties for oil product imports to cover shortages with deliveries from Belarus and the Baltic states.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no panic. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed it would cover unsatisfied offers. It showed its corridor and made it clear that it will be possible to buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," another dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has vowed not to allow abrupt changes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and said it would defend a rate of about 5.05 per dollar. That rate was set on April 21, a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  jolted markets by allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise by about 3 percent in one trading day.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050606e1660011r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
