\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Ukraine c. bank sells dollars for 2nd straight day  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Olena Horodetska  \par \uc2 467 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Juni 2005\par 14:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds c. bank comments)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, June 1 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday for the second straight day to sell dollars and support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and said it saw no real reason for any change in its rate in the near term.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars at 5.06 to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  against demand for dollars stemming from growing fuel imports and the global strength of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 But Serhiy Yaremenko, deputy \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chairman, said he saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  remaining steady in the near future.  \par \par \uc2 "I believe there is no real reason for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate to change in the near future," he told parliament during a debate on government budget policies for next year.  \par \par \uc2 "Any country tries to achieve stability of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate. It speaks about economic stability."  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fixed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.05 per dollar since April 21 when it jolted markets by allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise by about 3 percent in a single trading day.  \par \par \uc2 Over the last two months the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly to buy dollars and curb a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> is generally seen as undervalued due to a robust current account surplus, strong exports and a steady inflow of foreign investment into Ukraine's debt market.  \par \par \uc2 The trend changed this week, however, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to start dollar sales on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Loads of oil money is working on the market right now. People are buying fuel and need dollars," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 "Look what is happening globally with the dollar and euro. Exporters are unwilling to sell dollars and delay things."  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine was hit last month by rising fuel prices and shortages. The government scrapped duties for oil product imports to help cover shortages and stabilise prices with deliveries from Belarus and the Baltic countries.  \par \par \uc2 The euro hit 7-1/2 month lows against the dollar <EUR=> following France's rejection of the EU constitution.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said dollar shortages would probably ease as non-residents would purchase \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to pay for government treasury bonds.  \par \par \uc2 The Finance Ministry sold treasury notes worth a total of about $50 million at Tuesday's auctions. Bankers said non-residents actively bought 511-day papers which yielded 5.62 percent. Yields on three-year papers were steady at 6.3 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at about 5.065/0725 on Wednesday compared with 5.075/5.095 the previous trading day.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market rigidly. Commercial banks are not allowed to buy and sell hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same trading day.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050601e1610019b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
