\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank sells dollars -1st time in 2 months  \b0\par\par\uc2 326 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Mai 2005\par 16:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (adds details, quotes)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 31 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to sell dollars at 5.06 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in two months as demand for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spiked due to rising imports, dealers said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly over the past two months to buy dollars and curb a rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Tuesday's action was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since April 5 to sell the dollar and prop the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Demand was big. Usually demand builds after the weekend. Besides our economy is relying on imports at the moment," a dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  <UAH=> is seen as undervalued due to a robust current account surplus, strong exports and a steady inflow of foreign investment into Ukraine's debt market.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  jolted the market last month by fixing the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 5.05, up from 5.19 in a single day. It has since vowed to defend the new rate and regularly bought dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout May.  \par \par \uc2 But dealers said the trend had started to change in recent days due to rising imports.  \par \par \uc2 The government scrapped duties for oil product imports earlier this month to alleviate domestic fuel shortages and stabilise prices. It also cut import duties for meat products and some other foodstuffs.  \par \par \uc2 One dealer estimated demand was about $20 million higher than supply on Tuesday and the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at about 5.075/5.095 to the dollar. Deals were concluded at between 5.05 and 5.08 per dollar, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers expected the market to calm down later in the week.  \par \par \uc2 Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is rigidly controlled by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Banks are not allowed both to sell and buy \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the same trading day.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 UKRAINE\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050531e15v001ju\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
