\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-Ukraine  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  seen firming to 4.85/dlr by yr-end  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Toni Vorobyova  \par \uc2 651 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 2005\par 13:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, May 19 (Reuters) - The Ukrainian \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will probably make modest gains against the dollar in the second half of the year as inflationary pressures prompt the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to loosen controls on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Reuters poll shows.  \par \par \uc2 The National Bank of Ukraine (NBU) stunned markets on April 20 by allowing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to jump three percent in one day, effectively abandoning a 5-year-old peg of 5.30 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar. It has since \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  roughly around a new target level of 5.05. All but two of the 15 analysts surveyed May 16-19 expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to appreciate further this year. The median forecasts showed it at 5.03 per dollar <UAH=> at the end of June -- broadly unchanged from current levels -- but strengthening to 4.85 by the end of 2005.  \par \par \uc2 "The NBU should be able to hold its current peg for the next month or two, but with inflationary pressure building and the the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  massively undervalued at its current exchange rate, we expect a further appreciation later in the year," said Rory MacFarquhar at Goldman Sachs in Moscow.  \par \par \uc2 To curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's appreciation the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  prints \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and bought over $4 billion in the first four months of the year.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said it could not ignore the inflationary pressures of such active \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially as \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new liberal government hopes to cut inflation to single digits this year from 12.3 percent in 2004.  \par \par \uc2 "We believe that unless there is a particularly good harvest, which induces a decline in inflation, the government hasn't done enough in terms of combatting inflation and there will be no option but to allow a certain additional appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sonal Desai at DrKW in Milan.  \par \par \uc2 FREE FLOAT FAR AWAY  \par \par \uc2 Although analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to allow the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to firm in coming months, they do not think it will completely abandon the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to market forces just yet.  \par \par \uc2 "Ukraine still has a long way to go before its financial system and markets mature enough to allow a full flotation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  and it is not a given that the country will manage to stay the current pro-reform course all the way," said Tomasz Balamut at WestLB in Warsaw.  \par \par \uc2 Setting the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  free would probably prompt a big rally. But with up to half of Ukraine's bank reserves held in dollars, a big appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar could effectively slash the value of many people's savings.  \par \par \uc2 Five of the analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be fully floating as soon as next year after parliamentary elections due in early 2006. Four said it could happen in 2007 or 2008, five said it would take longer and one gave no answer. Even with the forecast appreciation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is set to remain seriously undervalued, the poll showed. The median estimate put the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's current fair value at 4.00 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "Our view is that it is highly undervalued -- probably by as much as 30 percent. But the fair value is pretty hard to know given that we haven't had any time when we've had a free float," said Lars Christensen at Danske Bank in Copenhagen.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen staying fairly stable against the euro in coming months. Medians showed it at 6.38 per euro <EURUAH=> at the end of June and at 6.35 at the end of the year, compared to 6.35 on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 End year forecasts ranged from 5.70 to 6.86 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per euro and from 4.50 to 5.05 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-POLL-UKRAINE|LANGEN|ABN|M|D|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050519e15j0018f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
