\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine cbank buys dollars at 5.01 for 5th day.  \b0\par\par\uc2 305 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Mai 2005\par 15:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, May 4 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought dollars at 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the fifth consecutive trading day on Wednesday to curb the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise after last month's step-up revaluation, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said a steady inflow of dollars from investors in debt ahead of a treasury auction on Thursday forced the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again.  \par \par \uc2 Predominantly Orthodox \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2  celebrated Easter holidays from May 1 to May 3 which means funds had been locked up for the period creating delayed demand.  \par \par \uc2 "Western analysts see the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as undervalued and expect to see it trading at around 4.6 per dollar. It means non-residents can make profits on rate differences and an inflow of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from them is not stopping," a Ukrainian bank dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  marked the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  3 percent higher on April 20 yielding under pressure of strong capital inflows from debt investors and exporters.  \par \par \uc2 It has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  ever since to defend the new target rate of 5.05 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts, politicians, the International Monetary Fund and even some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials still see the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as undervalued.  \par \par \uc2 However, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh said there would be no further sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation, adding he saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's average rate at 5.1 per dollar this year.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said most deals were done at 5.0101 per dollar on Wednesday. They also said dollar supply would remain strong in coming months.  \par \par \uc2 "Maybe, if the finance ministry stops selling treasuries, non-residents will not be coming in that actively. But overall the dollar supply will be higher than demand in the nearest months."  \par \par \uc2 The finance ministry plans to sell three-and four-year government securities at auctions on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050504e154003eo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
