\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine c.bank promises to ease  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market controls.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalia Zinets  \par \uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2005\par 13:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Wraps central bankers, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 )  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced steps on Thursday to ease tight controls on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market after hefty capital inflows forced it to revalue the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week.  \par \par \uc2 Volodymyr Stelmakh, head of the National Bank of Ukraine, told a news conference that new rules - including allowing market participants to buy and sell in a single session - would come into force after the holiday at the beginning of May.  \par \par \uc2 "The document has been already worked out. Tomorrow it will be submited to the Justice Ministry. I think it will take effect after May holidays," Stelmakh told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 Predominantly Christian Orthodox Ukraine will celebrate Easter on May 1 and Victory Day on May 9.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  abandoned its longstanding peg of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar last week. It allowed the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise by 3 percent against the dollar on April 20 after heavy bidding by foreign investors at a treasury bond auction.  \par \par \uc2 Since then Stelmakh has drawn a new line in the sand, vowing to defend a central rate of 5.05 to the dollar this year - up from the old rate of 5.30 which had been in force since 2000.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  again on the local market on Thursday, buying dollars at a rate of 5.01 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the third day running.  \par \par \uc2 EASIER RULES  \par \par \uc2 Emerging markets investors zeroed in on Ukraine after the "Orange Revolution" swept a pro-reform leadership to power. Non-residents now hold 6 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  ($1.2 billion) or about 50 percent of all outstanding government debt.  \par \par \uc2 That has strained the draconian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market controls imposed after the 1998 financial crash in neighbouring Russia and the financial community has clamoured for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be allowed to float more freely.  \par \par \uc2 Valery Lytvytsky, Stelmakh's chief adviser, told Reuters earlier on Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may extend \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading hours and allow market participants to buy second-tier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the possibility of abolishing a 1.5 percent transaction tax on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases, which goes towards the state pension fund, would depend on an improvement in Ukraine's budget situation. Non-residents are exempt but residents are not.  \par \par \uc2 "At the moment the situation is rather strained, but I would not rule out the possibility of abolishing this 1.5 percent tax for residents - if the budget balance turns positive," Lytvytsky said in an interview.  \par \par \uc2 Echoing Stelmakh, Lytvytsky said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would allow small fluctuations of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  around its new target rate of 5.05 to the dollar, but would not tolerate major volatility.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't want this to be interpreted as a new fixed rate. We will in future observe the principle of flexibility," he said. "Fluctuations will be possible but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will seek to prevent sharp moves from happening."  \par \par \uc2 Lytvytsky said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained fundamentally undervalued, but argued it was vital to move slowly to allow Ukraine's population - long used to a stable exchange rate - to adjust. Up to half of Ukraine's bank deposits are in dollars.  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Douglas Busvine).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050428e14s00aia\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
