\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -High yielders broadly soft, zloty under pressure.  \b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 April 2005\par 12:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  LONDON, April 28 (Reuters) - The Polish zloty led a broadly soft tone for emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, with lower domestic interest rates and political jitters still applying downward pressure.   \par \par \uc2  Global market uncertainty and nerves before first quarter growth figures in the United States at 1230 GMT kept the tone cautious in most high-yield \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2  The zloty was anchored close to five-month lows against the euro, after falling the previous session on speculation, later confirmed, of a 50 basis point interest rate cut from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  which took the key rate to 5.50 percent.   \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market quickly refocused its attention on political risk in Poland with parliament due to vote next week on whether to dissolve itself, paving the way for early elections in June.   \par \par \uc2  "We had a bit of a relief rally to 4.21 after the rate cut, but it was reversed very quickly. People still see significant political risk ahead of next week's vote in parliament and the referendums on the EU constitution," said one UK bank trader.   \par \par \uc2  Investors are also concerned about a potential delay to the timetable for central European countries joining the euro if France and the Netherlands reject the EU constitution in upcoming referendums.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par By 0945 GMT, the zloty traded at 4.2550 to the euro  from 4.2350 late\par on Wednesday and at 3.2928 to the dollar        from 3.2662.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The zloty is about 10 percent lower against the euro since the\par beginning of March, but there's still little appetite from foreigners\par or domestic players to put fresh risk on the table," the trader added.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "In view of the current uncertainty worldwide, the risk reward does not\par justify going long zloty," he said, pointing to the 4.29 level as a\par potential near-term upside target.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Hungarian forint also headed lower, weakening beyond 250 per euro\par in line with the broadly softer regional tone. It traded at 250.40.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par RAND EASES\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South African rand tracked the broadly softer tone in high-yield\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but held inside established ranges before the U.S. growth\par data later in the session.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market shrugged off further evidence that inflationary pressures in\par South Africa are picking up. March producer prices had a\par higher-than-expected annual rate of 1.9 percent in March, up from 1.2\par percent the previous month.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts had already scaled back expectations for a rate cut at the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's next policy meeting in June after March consumer price\par data on Tuesday showed core inflation picking up from February's record\par lows.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The data confirms the trend that inflation has bottomed, but no\par inflationary pressures are suggested to concern the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said\par Tania Kotsos, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  analyst at Royal Bank of Canada. "The 0.7\par percent rise in imported prices was the highest since 2003 and a\par reflection of rand weakness in March, but its still well below trend."\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Kotsos said the impact on the rand was likely to be muted, with the\par market more closely focused on the external environment and the\par performance of the dollar. The rand was around 0.5 percent down at 6.08\par to the dollar .\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ukraine\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again at around 5.01 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 hryvnias\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  per\par dollar , according to Kiev dealers, in line with comments from a bank\par adviser that it would look to keep the rate steady roughly around 5.05\par in 2005.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050428e14s008yc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
