\par\par \b \uc2 Ukraine's c.bank will allow stronger  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2 -aide.   \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2005\par 11:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 KIEV, April 14 (Reuters) - Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow a gradual appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb rising inflation and support economic recovery, a senior adviser to the bank's chairman said.   \par \par \uc2 The International Monetary Fund believes the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which trades at about 5.25 per dollar, is undervalued given a record current account surplus and strong exports.   \par \par \uc2 "We support a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," Valery Lytvytsky told reporters late on Thursday. "But there will be no plunge in the dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not stop \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rigidly controls \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It is a key buyer and seller of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sets the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by administrative means.   \par \par \uc2 The government, which rose to power amid street protests late last year, has also urged the bank to ease its grip on the market and let the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  float more freely. The government sees a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a key measure against inflation.   \par \par \uc2 "A stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not a panacea," Lytvytsky said. "The rate should not be blocking credits. The rate should not hinder exports and domestic production. It should help competition."   \par \par \uc2 Lytvytsky gave no level for the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate by the end of the year. Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko said last month she expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise to about 5.0 per dollar by the end of the year.   \par \par \uc2 Ukraine is awash with hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to booming exports of steel and chemicals and foreign fund inflows on the domestic debt market.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has engaged in considerable \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the interbank market so far this year to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It has bought over $3.1 billion since the start of the year compared with $2.6 billion throughout 2004.   \par \par \uc2 Exporters had until this month been obliged to sell at least 50 percent of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings on the interbank market but the measure was scrapped from April 1.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050415e14f009km\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
