\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ukraine's Yushchenko sees  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2  rising in '05.  \b0\par\par\uc2 351 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 14:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 (Ccombines stories, adds quotes, details)  \par \par \uc2 KIEV, March 29 (Reuters) - Ukrainian President Viktor Yushchenko said on Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would appreciate this year, but made no predictions on its future level.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko, who launched the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1996 during his six-year stint as head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the supply of dollars on the interbank market was "colossal" at the moment.  \par \par \uc2 "It is most likely that we can expect appreciation of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Yushchenko told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is currently traded at about 5.29 per dollar on Ukraine's interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Prime Minister Yulia Tymoshenko has said the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  could rise to about 5.0 by the end of the year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which tightly controls the interbank market, is trying to curb any \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to buy out dollars. \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy is export-reliant.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought about $1.6 billion in the first two months of the year compared to $2.6 billion throughout 2004.  \par \par \uc2 The government has expressed concern that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar purchases might fuel inflation this year and last week ordered the rescinding of a rule requiring exporters to sell at least 50 percent of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings.  \par \par \uc2 Ministers have urged the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give its required consent to the change. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has so far been unwilling, saying financial stability remained fragile.  \par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman, speaking by telephone, said Tymoshenko, accompanied by senior ministers, had met \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chairman Volodymyr Stelmakh on Tuesday to discuss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy. She gave no details.  \par \par \uc2 Yushchenko said the meeting was needed to clear up discrepancies between statements issued by ministers and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past two months.  \par \par \uc2 "I think that after today's meeting of the National Bank head, the prime minister and the economy minister a position will at last be formed and publicly stated," he said.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the basis of these policies should be formed by the National bank taking account of the economy ministry's position."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050329e13t00af6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
