\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Ukraine floats  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 401 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Februar 2000\par 18:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KIEV, Feb 21 (Reuters) - Ukraine will untie its \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a rigid trading band against the dollar and allow it to float freely, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government said on Monday in a statement which confirmed market expectations. \par \par \uc2  The more liberal \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy meets demands of international lenders who have insisted on the abolition of administrative restrictions on Ukraine's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and confirms a de facto policy which began last year. \par \par \uc2  But the bank and government promised to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's cabinet of ministers and National Bank consider that under the current circumstances a floating rate will be the most realistic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and government said. \par \par \uc2  The move has largely been expected since it is an official acknowledgment of a policy in effect since the second half of last year, when the bank, short on reserves, let the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  break the band at that time of 3.4-4.6 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Some experts said the printing of large amounts of money by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  before last year's presidential election contributed to the fall. \par \par \uc2  On Monday the official rate was set at 5.5748 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  per dollar and the government expects an average rate of 5.78 this year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , whose reserves stood at just over $1 billion at the start of this year, became an active buyer of hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  last year, purchasing more than $700 million. \par \par \uc2  On Monday authourites said they would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the stability of the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  was threatened. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government and the National Bank intend to watch closely tendencies of economic development and events on the money market to defend the monetary system and...ensure the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate which helps economic growth," the statement said. \par \par \uc2  The government and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected the floating rate to help Ukraine's integration into the world economy, support the competitiveness of domestic goods, raise the profitability of local companies and save \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves. \par \par \uc2  Cash-short Ukraine, which faces crushing foreign debt payments worth more than $3.1 billion this year, is seeking renewed financial assistance from the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  Ukraine introduced the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 1.76 per dollar in September 1996 and the following year established a corridor. \par \par \uc2  ((Dmitry Solovyov, Kiev Newsroom, +380 44 244 9150 kiev.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw2l06udb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
