\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2  C.bank to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  on t-bill market June. \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juni 1998\par 13:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KIEV, June 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to participate actively on the former Soviet republic's primary and secondary treasury-bill markets in June, bank chairman Viktor Yushchenko said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  "We have reserved the possibility of conducting active \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the secondary market in June," Yushchenko told reporters. "I think June requires detailed work from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and money market and we will be interested in working very actively with our portfolio." \par \par \uc2  He confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would purchase new treasury bills on the primary market in June, using money it had earned on the market so far this year. \par \par \uc2  Yushchenko declined to say how much money the bank would spend on the secondary market, where yields are higher than on the primary market. Three-month paper earned 57.73 percent and 12-month paper was at 53.30 percent at most recent primary auctions. \par \par \uc2  He said earlier this month the bank had sold 110 million \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  ($53.5 million) worth of paper on the secondary market between January and April this year. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimate that of one billion \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2  which the finance ministry must repay in maturing paper this month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is owed 30 percent of the total and non-resident buyers are owed 60 percent. They also say the bank has been the main buyer of bills in 1998. ((Natalya Zinets, Kiev Newsroom, +380 44 244 9150 kiev.newsroom@reuters.com)) ($ = 2.0579 \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 ). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6203rol\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
