\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine \highlight\uc2 's c.bank says  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  to help  \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 488 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  KIEV, Nov 13 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the secondary interbank market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  once in recent days and may do so again, bank chief Viktor Yushchenko said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The leadership reserves the right, depending on the situation on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Treasury-bill markets, to use such an instrument, possibly, on occasion," he told a news conference. \par \par \uc2  "Like any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  we must guard our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and we are fulfilling this function today." \par \par \uc2  Yushchenko announced in December 1996 that the bank would only work on the Ukrainian Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange this year. He confirmed in April that this policy had not changed. \par \par \uc2  But asked if this had changed recently, Yushchenko said: "This \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not happen several times but once a few days ago...In today's situation I cannot say that this was the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Ukraine\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one and only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ". \par \par \uc2  He made clear he saw the problem with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as temporary and linked to financial market turmoil abroad. \par \par \uc2  "I do not think this (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) was enough by itself to calm \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and T-bill markets once and for all. Our thesis that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not consider it expedient to work on the secondary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is still actual," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being held within a range of 1.70 to 1.90 to the dollar this year, which is due to ease to 1.75 to 1.95 over the first half of 1998. \par \par \uc2  Yushchenko confirmed that the bank had dug into its reserves in September when markets were weak. A typical situation on the interbank exchange recently has been zero demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We are in a controllable regime, but I cannot say we do not use the bank's reserves. Of course we use them...and it would be surprising if Ukraine was unaffected, when \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets all around it are having colossal problems costing billions of dollars," he added. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the bank sold a big volume of \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnias\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but Yushchenko would give no details of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In September and October the bank was forced to meet big demand for dollars on the Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Exchange, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 hryvnia\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at 1.8770 to the dollar on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers linked this to the fact that foreigners' participation in the T-bill market had fallen back recently. \par \par \uc2  Yushchenko declined to say what reserves were. Ukrayinskiy Novyny said net reserves fell from $678 million on September 1 to $248 million a month later and had only recovered slightly by October 29 to $282.5 million. \par \par \uc2  "Since September, movement of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves has stabilised. We did not have any serious growth, but we had no serious losses," Yushchenko said. \par \par \uc2  --Natalya Zinets, Kiev Newsroom, +380 44 244 9150 \par \par \uc2  e-mail:kiev.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtbd02mls\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
